## Submission format (machine-checked)

The mandated format is a FACT from the RFT, not a choice at build time. `eng_lint.py` reads this
table: an artefact built in a format the buyer does not accept is an error under `4_final/`, and a
volume with no sections written is reported before someone discovers it at 11pm.

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| volumes | <n — one file per volume> |
| file formats accepted | <e.g. docx, pdf> |
| paper | <e.g. A4> |
| minimum font | <e.g. Arial 10> |
| separator page between sub-sections | <required / not required> |

Sections live one directory per volume — `3_drafting/sections/v1/`, `v2/`, … — so each volume
renders into its own file and a volume nobody has started is visible.

## Volume / section map
| § | Response section (per RFP format) | Answers Req IDs | Also answers (scored here too) | Win-theme(s) | Evidence (BR-nnn / A-nnn) | Owner | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| V1.1 | <section title from RFP> | R-00x, R-00y | R-0zz | theme-1 | BR-003, A-001 | <name> | outline |

**Status key:** `outline` → `draft` → `red-teamed` → `final`.

**One requirement, two scored places.** A real tender grades the same requirement twice — a
roadmap under *Deliverables* and again under *Methodology*. Name the primary section in
`Answers Req IDs` and the second one in *Also answers*; do not drop the row or duplicate the
answer wholesale.

## Rows that are NOT written sections — and the control that owns each

Some matrix rows are obligations on the bid *process* or terms accepted by submitting, not
questions to answer in prose. Mapping those onto an invented section is how a compliance matrix
starts lying. Give each a named control instead — an artefact someone signs off:

| Control | Rows it owns | What the control is |
|---|---|---|
| Submission control sheet (bid manager's pre-flight) | R-00x | deadline, volume split, font/page limits, no qualified language |
| Clarification register | R-00x | the written-query log and its deadline |
| Commercial sign-off | R-00x | validity period, rates adequacy, withholding tax |
| Partner-level contract acceptance | R-00x | terms accepted as issued, with background IP scheduled |

Coverage is machine-checked: `eng_lint.py` errors if a matrix row appears **nowhere** in this
file. Where it lands — a section or a control — is this file's judgement, not the linter's.

